{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>His firstborn bullock, majesty is his.</b> Because he mentioned produce, he likened the tribe to an ox, in the manner of what is written (Proverbs 14:4): ״ורב תבואות בכח שור״, and he mentioned 'firstborn' because he was the firstborn of Rachel; and ״קרני ראם קרניו״ — his horns are the horns of a re'em — in the strength of the myriads of Ephraim." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: ״בכור שורו הדר לו״ — there were given to Joseph the righteous two middot, Netsah and Hod, and this is what it says: ״בכור שורו הדר לו״ — for הדר is Netsah, which is on the right, and Hod, which is on the left, is alluded to in שור (ox), for there is the form of an ox, as is known in the Kabbalah. And because these two middot were given to him, they likened him to two things, to an ox and to a re'em: to an ox corresponding to Hod, and to a re'em corresponding to Netsah. And you should know that from there the prayer of David was heard, as is said (Psalms 22:22): ״ומקרני רמים עניתני״; and likewise two tribes went forth from him — the tribe of Ephraim, which was named for פריה ורביה (fruitfulness), which is the matter of compassion, and the second, the tribe of Manasseh, which was named for השכחה (forgetting), which is of the matter of judgment."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:17.712033978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}